          "code": "PARALLEL_1774435185377",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769413666759",
          "id": "1774435185376",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "PARALLEL"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Intent Classifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769413609418"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_INTENT_CLASSIFIER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1774435194247",
          "id": "1769448897968",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769448897970_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intent classification engine for a payments assistant.\n\nYour task is to analyze the user's message and chat history, then return a structured JSON output.\n\n### Chat History\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n\n### User Message\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n### Intent Definitions\n\n1. SHOW_NEW_CASH_OUTFLOW\n   - The user is asking to show, generate, display, calculate, or explain what the new cash outflow looks like.\n   - Examples:\n     - \"Show me my new cash flow\"\n     - \"What do my payments look like if I use VCC?\"\n     - \"How does my cash outflow change with supply chain financing?\"\n     - \"Calculate cash outflow for the best external DD program\"\n\n2. FOLLOW_UP_ON_NEW_CASH_OUTFLOW\n   - The user is asking a follow-up question about cash flow that has already been presented.\n   - Examples:\n     - \"Why is week 4 zero?\"\n     - \"Can you explain the last week amount?\"\n     - \"Why did the payment move to week 6?\"\n\n### Payment Program Type Identification\n\nIf the intent is SHOW_NEW_CASH_OUTFLOW, identify the underlying payment program type mentioned by the user.\n\nUse fuzzy matching and natural language understanding.\n\nMap user references as follows:\n\n- Supply Chain Financing → SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING\n  Examples:\n  - \"SCF\"\n  - \"supply chain finance\"\n  - \"supply chain financing\"\n  - \"supplier financing\"\n\n- Virtual Credit Card → VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\n  Examples:\n  - \"VCC\"\n  - \"virtual card\"\n  - \"virtual credit card\"\n  - \"credit card payments\"\n\n- Dynamic Discounting → DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING\n  Examples:\n  - \"DD\"\n  - \"dynamic discounting\"\n  - \"early payment discount\"\n  - \"pay early for discount\"\n  - \"discounting program\"\n\nIf no payment program type can be confidently identified, return NONE.\n\n### Program Category Identification\n\nIf the intent is SHOW_NEW_CASH_OUTFLOW, identify whether the user is referring to an external or signed/internal program category.\n\nUse fuzzy matching and natural language understanding.\n\nMap user references as follows:\n\n- external → EXTERNAL\n  Examples:\n  - \"external program\"\n  - \"external DD program\"\n  - \"best external VCC program\"\n\n- signed or internal → SIGNED\n  Important:\n  - \"signed\" and \"internal\" mean the same thing.\n  - If the user says \"internal\", return programCategory as SIGNED.\n  Examples:\n  - \"signed program\"\n  - \"signed DD program\"\n  - \"signed VCC programs\"\n  - \"internal program\"\n  - \"internal DD program\"\n  - \"best internal VCC program\"\n\nIf no program category can be confidently identified, return ALL.\n\n### Exact Payment Program Name Extraction\n\nExtract `paymentProgramName` ONLY when the user mentions a specific branded financing program, provider, or named offering.\n\nA valid `paymentProgramName` is a distinctive program/provider name such as:\n- \"APAC Supplier Discount Program\"\n- \"Corporate Virtual Card Program\"\n- \"JPMorgan SCF\"\n- \"Taulia\"\n- \"PrimeRevenue\"\n\nRules:\n- Scan both the current User Message and the Chat History for a specific branded program/provider name.\n- Prefer the closest noun phrase immediately after verbs or prepositions such as:\n  \"adopting\", \"using\", \"with\", \"under\", \"via\", \"through\", \"for\"\n- Capture the complete consecutive phrase, including modifying adjectives such as \"Corporate\", \"APAC\", \"Global\", or provider names.\n- Preserve the exact wording and casing from the user message.\n- Do not confuse the program name with supplier name, business unit, currency, program category, or payment program type.\n- If multiple candidate names exist, choose the most specific branded financing/program label.\n- If no specific branded program/provider name is found, return null.\n\nImportant exclusion rules:\n- Do NOT set `paymentProgramName` to generic payment program type phrases.\n- Generic type/category words should be used only to identify `paymentProgramType` and `programCategory`, not `paymentProgramName`.\n\nDo NOT return these as `paymentProgramName`:\n- \"DD\"\n- \"Dynamic Discounting\"\n- \"dynamic discounting program\"\n- \"external DD program\"\n- \"signed DD program\"\n- \"internal DD program\"\n- \"VCC\"\n- \"VCC program\"\n- \"SCF\"\n- \"SCF program\"\n- \"best external DD program\"\n- \"best signed DD program\"\n- \"best internal DD program\"\n- \"best VCC program\"\n- \"external program\"\n- \"signed program\"\n- \"internal program\"\n\n### Any / Best / Unspecified Program Rule\n\nIf the user asks for a program by type or category but does not name a specific branded program/provider, set:\n- `paymentProgramName` = null\n- `isAnyProgramRequested` = true\n\nThis applies when the user uses phrases such as:\n- \"any\"\n- \"any one\"\n- \"a\"\n- \"an\"\n- \"some\"\n- \"best\"\n- \"top\"\n- \"recommended\"\n- \"optimal\"\n- \"highest savings\"\n- \"lowest cost\"\n- \"available\"\n\nExamples:\n\n1. User message:\n   \"Calculate cash outflow for the best external DD program for business unit Vision Operations in currency USD.\"\n\n   Output fields:\n   paymentProgramType = \"DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING\"\n   programCategory = \"EXTERNAL\"\n   paymentProgramName = null\n   isAnyProgramRequested = true\n\n2. User message:\n   \"Calculate cash outflow for any signed VCC program.\"\n\n   Output fields:\n   paymentProgramType = \"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\"\n   programCategory = \"SIGNED\"\n   paymentProgramName = null\n   isAnyProgramRequested = true\n\n3. User message:\n   \"Calculate cash outflow for the best internal DD program.\"\n\n   Output fields:\n   paymentProgramType = \"DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING\"\n   programCategory = \"SIGNED\"\n   paymentProgramName = null\n   isAnyProgramRequested = true\n\n4. User message:\n   \"Calculate cash outflow for APAC Supplier Discount Program.\"\n\n   Output fields:\n   paymentProgramName = \"APAC Supplier Discount Program\"\n   isAnyProgramRequested = false\n\n5. User message:\n   \"Calculate cash outflow for JPMorgan SCF.\"\n\n   Output fields:\n   paymentProgramName = \"JPMorgan SCF\"\n   isAnyProgramRequested = false\n\n6. User message:\n   \"Show me what my new cash flow looks like if I use any one virtual card program.\"\n\n   Output fields:\n   paymentProgramType = \"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\"\n   paymentProgramName = null\n   isAnyProgramRequested = true\n\n### Supplier Identification & Validation\n\nAnalyze the user's message and chat history to determine if they are requesting information for specific suppliers rather than all suppliers.\n\nIf specific suppliers are mentioned, such as:\n- \"Show me VCC for Dell\"\n- \"What about cash flow for Advanced Network Devices?\"\n\nThen:\n1. Extract the requested supplier name(s) from the user message or chat history.\n2. Cross-reference the extracted name(s) against the suppliers listed in the `Payable Balances` data block provided below.\n3. If a match IS found:\n   - Set `isSpecificSupplierRequested` to true.\n   - Set `requestedSupplierNotFound` to false.\n   - Add the exact matching name(s) from the `Payable Balances` data to the `requestedSuppliers` array.\n4. If a specific supplier IS requested, but NO match is found in the data:\n   - Set `requestedSupplierNotFound` to true.\n   - Set `isSpecificSupplierRequested` to false.\n   - Leave `requestedSuppliers` empty [].\n5. If NO specific supplier is requested:\n   - Set `isSpecificSupplierRequested` to false.\n   - Set `requestedSupplierNotFound` to false.\n   - Leave `requestedSuppliers` empty [].\n\n### Output Rules\n\n- Always return valid JSON.\n- Do not include explanations or extra text outside the JSON block.\n- Use EXACT enum values for intent, paymentProgramType, and programCategory.\n- Use programCategory = SIGNED when the user says either \"signed\" or \"internal\".\n- Never output INTERNAL as programCategory.\n- If intent is FOLLOW_UP_ON_NEW_CASH_OUTFLOW:\n  - Set paymentProgramType to NONE.\n  - Set programCategory to ALL.\n  - Set paymentProgramName to null.\n  - Set isAnyProgramRequested to false.\n- The requestedSuppliers array must ONLY contain string values that map to actual suppliers in the Payable Balances data.\n- Never infer a branded payment program name from a generic type, category, or ranking phrase.\n\n### Output Format\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"<SHOW_NEW_CASH_OUTFLOW | FOLLOW_UP_ON_NEW_CASH_OUTFLOW>\",\n  \"paymentProgramType\": \"<SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING | VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD | DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING | NONE>\",\n  \"programCategory\": \"<EXTERNAL | SIGNED | ALL>\",\n  \"paymentProgramName\": \"<Exact string of the specific program name | null>\",\n  \"isAnyProgramRequested\": <boolean>,\n  \"isSpecificSupplierRequested\": <true | false>,\n  \"requestedSupplierNotFound\": <true | false>,\n  \"requestedSuppliers\": [\"<Supplier Name 1>\", \"<Supplier Name 2>\"]\n}\n\n### Payable Balances\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.payablesBalance}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"CashOutflowIntentClassification\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\n    \"intent\",\n    \"paymentProgramType\",\n    \"programCategory\",\n    \"paymentProgramName\",\n    \"isAnyProgramRequested\",\n    \"isSpecificSupplierRequested\",\n    \"requestedSupplierNotFound\",\n    \"requestedSuppliers\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"intent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Identifies whether the user is requesting to show new cash outflow or asking a follow-up question on an already presented cash outflow.\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"SHOW_NEW_CASH_OUTFLOW\",\n        \"FOLLOW_UP_ON_NEW_CASH_OUTFLOW\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"paymentProgramType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Identifies the underlying payment program type referenced by the user when requesting to show new cash outflow.\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING\",\n        \"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\",\n        \"DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING\",\n        \"NONE\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"programCategory\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Identifies whether the program category referenced by the user is external, signed, or all if not specified.\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"EXTERNAL\",\n        \"SIGNED\",\n        \"ALL\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"paymentProgramName\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The exact, specific name of the financing program or provider extracted from the user message or chat history (e.g., 'Citi VCC', 'Taulia'). Returns null if no specific branded name is found.\"\n    },\n    \"isAnyProgramRequested\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"True if the user explicitly asks for 'any', 'any one', or 'a' program of a specific type without naming a specific branded program. Otherwise, false.\"\n    },\n    \"isSpecificSupplierRequested\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"Indicates whether the user specifically requested cash outflow data for one or more specific suppliers that exist in the payable balances data.\"\n    },\n    \"requestedSupplierNotFound\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"Indicates whether the user requested a specific supplier but no exact or high-confidence match was found in the payable balances data.\"\n    },\n    \"requestedSuppliers\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"An array containing the exact, formatted supplier names extracted and validated against the Payable Balances data. Empty if no specific supplier was requested or matched.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
